claimed: http-request-query -- fix the query-string gap BACKLOG filed while landing okay-script-storefront-example. Not "no query-string support at all" as first written: okay.http.Server (JDK HttpExchange-based) already preserves the query string in Request.url via getRequestURI().toString(); only okay-jetty is broken, because Jetty.scala requestOf builds url from org.eclipse.jetty.server.Request.getPathInContext(req) (path only). Fix: use req.getHttpURI.getPathQuery instead -- verified in the Jetty 12 sources (HttpURI.UriImpl.getPathQuery: path if no query, else path+"?"+query) it is a strict superset (existing no-query routes see the identical string) and no ContextHandler/context-path mounting is used anywhere in Jetty.scala, so getPathInContext and getHttpURI.getPath coincide today -- this is a pure fix, not a behavior change for existing routes. Add a real test proving Jetty now round-trips a query string the way okay.http.Server already does.
